# Aiko Desktop Pet — optional local configuration
#
# You do NOT need an .env file to run Aiko.
# No API keys, login details, AI model settings or cloud configuration exist.
# The only supported setting is AIKO_SAVE_PATH.
#
# To use a custom location:
#   1. Copy this file to .env in the project root.
#   2. Set AIKO_SAVE_PATH to a FILE path (not merely a folder).
#   3. Restart Aiko.
#
# Examples (choose one, remove the leading "# "):
# AIKO_SAVE_PATH=C:/Users/YourName/Documents/Aiko/state.sqlite3
# AIKO_SAVE_PATH=./local-data/aiko-state.sqlite3
#
# Existing .json paths remain import aliases: the matching .sqlite3 becomes
# active, while the original JSON and its unchanged backup are preserved.
#
# Relative paths are resolved from the project root. Paths with spaces can be
# wrapped in single or double quotes. Existing OS environment variables win.
#
# Leaving this blank preserves Aiko's normal platform-specific save location.
AIKO_SAVE_PATH=
